{
  "configuration_id": "config_003",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_002 (rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) achieved the best result so far (acc=0.591, F1=0.573), a substantial +10.6% improvement over singleprofile (config_001, acc=0.485). This confirms multiprofile aggregation is a critical design lever. Uncertainty: We have only tested avgpool as the aggregation method; it is unknown whether a transformer-based aggregation would further improve performance or whether simple averaging is already near-optimal. This experiment (config_003) isolates the aggregation variable by changing only avgpool→transformer while holding everything else at the known-best setting (rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000). Why this is the best next step: (1) It is a controlled one-variable extension of the current best result, maximizing information per experiment. (2) The aggregation method is a fundamental architectural choice that will propagate to all future multiprofile and multimodal experiments—knowing whether transformer adds value narrows the search space substantially. (3) If transformer significantly outperforms avgpool, it signals that learned aggregation is worth the extra complexity and should be prioritized in multimodal configs; if they are comparable, avgpool suffices and we can focus budget on RNA encoder choice and multimodal fusion. This reduces uncertainty about a high-impact design decision before committing experiments to the larger multimodal grid."
}

